From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:40:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: add Bananapi BPI-R4 Pro (8X, 4E, 4E-SFP)

Add device trees for the Bananapi BPI-R4 Pro router board family,
built around the MediaTek MT7988A (Filogic 880):

- mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dtsi: common board description:
  RT5190A PMIC, SPI-NAND with BL2/u-boot-env/Factory/FIP/UBI layout,
  internal 1G switch port, MaxLinear MxL86252 DSA switch with combo
  SerDes mux (ds-mux, SFP+ cage vs 10G PHY), two external 10G PHYs
  running Aeonsemi AS21x1x firmware, WAN-side ethernet SerDes mux,
  two SFP+ cages, PCA9545 I2C mux (INA226, PCF8563 RTC, EEPROMs,
  PCA9555 GPIO expander), per-slot buck rails modelled as fixed
  regulators (mPCIe A/B on the 2-lane ports via vpcie-supply, B-key
  SIM slot rails via the PCA9555 enables), PCIe lane-select GPIOs as
  pio hogs, PWM fan with thermal-zone cooling
  maps, four PCIe controllers (2x mPCIe, M.2 key-B, M.2 key-M).
- mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro.dts: BPI-R4 Pro 8X.
- mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-4e.dts: 4E variant. The WAN combo
  (10G SFP or 2.5G RJ45, no lane mux) is selected in software: this
  variant uses the internal 2.5G PHY on gmac1 and disables the
  combo's 10G SFP (sfp2). External 10G PHYs and both SerDes muxes are
  absent; the switch 10G port keeps the dedicated SFP LAN (sfp1).
- mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-4e-sfp.dts: 4E with SFP WAN - the same
  WAN combo selected the other way: gmac1 on SFP2 via 10GBase-R with
  the internal 2.5G PHY disabled; dedicated SFP LAN (sfp1) kept.
- mt7988a-pinctrl.dtsi: MT7988A pin groups used by the board.
- dtso overlays: eMMC (HS400) or SD boot device, PCF8563 RTC
  enablement, B-key slot routing on the 1L lane muxes (CN15/CN18)
  and MT7996 Wi-Fi with Factory-partition EEPROM data via NVMEM.

The device trees derive from the MediaTek SDK and Frank Wunderlich's
BPI-R4 Pro bring-up; original copyright and authorship headers are
preserved. Pairs with the mxl862xx, as21xxx and mtk_eth_soc NETSYS v3
driver patches in this series.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
